3D-ICE-Glass

The thermal solver in vendor/3d-ice is an unmodified snapshot of:
https://github.com/esl-epfl/3d-ice
Commit e0bb6850c5e446363e26936586d625270c87f224 (2025-12-01).

3D-ICE is copyright the Embedded Systems Laboratory, Ecole Polytechnique
Federale de Lausanne, and its contributing authors. Original notices and
COPYING are retained. The solver is distributed under GPL version 3 or later.
The bundled SuperLU MT archive and other third-party components retain their
original licensing, including notices inside the archive.
The preserved research SuperLU tuning source in provenance/research-build
retains its BSD license. Release builds tune only the extracted dependency's
U-factor allocation capacity; the pinned thermal engine is unchanged.

3D-ICE-Glass's release tools and supplied model inputs are released under the
GNU GPL version 3 or later. Academic source papers are cited for architectural
and calibration provenance; the model inputs are research representations,
not manufacturer CAD, certification, or official vendor models.

Documentation figures are extracted from the user-supplied manuscript,
"3D-ICE-Glass: Calibrated Thermal-Aware Floorplanning of Photonic Glass
Packages for Scalable AI". Figure numbers and source SHA-256 are recorded in
provenance/paper.json. Authors were omitted for blind review in that source.
A software license does not override rights in referenced third-party papers.
